[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-secrets.cxd — the keystore's page,
   repo-cx-platform-secrets.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 3).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the
   secrets suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-secrets
  [intro
    """A credential's value has exactly one place to be, and it is
       not your program. `cx-platform-secrets` is the minimal keystore:
       programs, feature documents, deployment documents and audit records
       carry a handle, `handle:<provider>/<path>`, and the value exists only
       inside this module's resolve seam and the one operation a consuming
       module hands it to. Everything that can reach a value is in this one
       repository, which is a boundary you can inspect, fork or replace."""]
  [body
    """What the operation receives is a `secret`: it computes — equal to the
       value it was resolved from, in constant time, unequal to any other —
       and it renders as `‹redacted›` at every emit boundary, so a log line,
       a canonical form or an error message cannot carry it out. A consumer
       the deployment's authorization rows do not grant is refused and
       nothing resolves; a malformed handle, an unbound provider and an
       absent value each refuse with their own code, in a fixed order the
       corpus pins."""]
  [body
    """Every resolution — granted or refused — writes one audit record naming
       the consuming module and the handle, never the value, through the
       [[store]]'s audit stream. Custody rises by a provider row: an `env`
       provider boots a development keystore and is refused in a served
       profile, a sealed store keeps values under AES-GCM beneath a master
       key file the keystore insists is mode 0600, rotation answers the
       active value inside its window and the successor after it, and a
       provider kind that could export a value is refused at boot. The `cx
       secrets` verbs stay in the front door's binary, because the binary is
       the front door's to build."""]
  [gives
    """One module of the platform group, a pure-CX package with no V code:
       `open`, `with-resolved`, the sealed store's put, rotate and list, and
       nothing that answers a value. It links to the reference page projected
       from its own documentation."""]
  [try
    """A keystore booted over an in-memory audit journal with one `env`
       provider, and a granted consumer handed the secret: emitted, it is
       the redaction marker; compared, it is equal to the value it came from
       and unequal to anything else. The `env` grant is the provider's, not
       the program's."""]
  [fixture id=secrets-003-the-seam-answers-a-secret-redacted-at-emit]
  [status
    """The keystore ships as a package: its one module is bundled into the
       build from the pin, its specification and corpus travel with it, and
       the connector kit resolves a gateway's credential through its seam at
       open."""]]
